A NOTE ON THE FIRST VERSION OF SEED 1, because it is the more useful finding.
The concurrency assertion was originally 'run two drains and check nothing is claimed twice'.
With FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED deleted it went red twice and then PASSED 8/8 — whether two
drains actually collide is timing. A check that only sometimes fails when the bug is present
has not been watched fail; it has had a good day. Replaced with an assertion of SKIP LOCKED's
actual semantics (a locked row is SKIPPED, not waited on), which is deterministic. Proof below
runs the same seed three times.

